<title>ITALY: Italy PM Prodi meets hard-left leader Bertinotti.</title>
<headline>Italy PM Prodi meets hard-left leader Bertinotti.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi met hard-left Communist Refoundation leader Fausto Bertinotti on Wednesday morning for talks centering on government privatisation plans.</p>
<p>Sources at the Marxist party, which opposes sell-offs in what it regards as nationally strategic sectors like energy and telecommunications, described the talks as difficult.</p>
<p>Also taking part in the hour-long meeting were Prodi's deputy Walter Veltroni, Treasury minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi and Industry minister Pierluigi Bersani.</p>
<p>Bertinotti's support in parliament ensures Prodi's centre-left government's majority.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
